                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its alright. The backdrop and atmosphere is really well done and reminds me of the old Roger Corman \"Poe series\" movies. The musket and blunderbuss are both cool and well represented with the reloading cycle and big plumes of smoke- but the sword absolutely sucks. Speaking of combat, while there [i]are[/i] audio cues when an enemy is nearby, the enemies are so small and SO fast, it's not scary- it's stupid. It's not like the \"fast zombies\" in something like '28 Days Later', it's like a crackhead running at you with a finger puppet and waving it around to give the illusion of movement. It's just jank. The finite resources (aside from the Bounty Hunter license) is also not great. It technically makes sense, but f*ck it anyway.\nIn conclusion; it's a great concept, cool design, great setting.. almost ruined by some cheap details. I get one guy alone worked on this, but.. still..",
